# config/defconfigs/robot-edge.config — RISC-V 64 / QEMU virt / Edge profile, Robot domain
#
# Target: QEMU virt riscv64 (development / CI): edge.config with the Robot
#         domain. Same values as qemu.config.
#
# Memory budget (rough):
#   Static tables (RFC-0023 edge): ~3-4 MiB
#   Kernel heap (KERNEL_HEAP_SIZE = 32768 KiB): 32 MiB
#   Lazy user stacks (MAX_TASKS=64 × 16 KiB demand-paged): ~1 MiB physical
#   Total worst-case: ~36-37 MiB  (well within QEMU 256 MiB RAM)
#
# Notable vs. defaults: ALL values are at Kconfig defaults.
#   ARCH=RISCV64, BOARD=QEMU, PROFILE=EDGE, TIMER_FREQ=10 MHz,
#   DRV_VIRTIO_BLK_NET=y (QEMU VirtIO), DRV_ML_INFERENCE=y,
#   WCET_BOUND_TIMER_ISR_US=0 (TCG SMP artefact mitigation).
#
# Used for: default `make` target, CI edge-profile build, quick iteration.
#
# Regenerate with:  make defconfig-robot-edge && make savedefconfig

# CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y (wave 11, DOMAIN): the robot worked example on the
# edge profile. The domain links the robot crates (kernel feature
# `domain-robot`); config/defconfigs/edge.config is the same profile with the
# default domain, Generic. The gate's edge rows build from this file.
CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y
